DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
$prompt = <<'PROMPT_0F40_E69F';
<p>0f40_e69f</p> <p><strong>Androgen insensitivity syndrome (AIS) </strong> is an X-linked recessive genetic disorder that is caused by a mutation in the AR gene for the human androgen receptor. This results in partial or complete inability of cells to respond to androgens. The disorder affects 1 in 20,000. Individuals affected with AIS have impaired development of male genitals and male secondary sexual characteristics at puberty. The defective gene for AIS is located on the long arm of chromosome X at position 11. </p><p><strong>Huntington's disease (HD) </strong> is an autosomal dominant genetic disorder that is caused by an increase in trinucleotide repeats in the HTT gene. This results in a mutated Huntington protein that is toxic to certain cell types, particularly brain cells. The disorder affects 1 in 10,000 adults of European descent. Individuals affected with HD have physical abilities that gradually worsen and mental abilities that decline into dementia. The defective gene for HD is located on the short arm of chromosome 4 at position 16.3. </p><p>A man (&male;) and a woman (&female;) are planning a family. The man (&male;) has AIS. The woman (&female;) is a carrier for AIS; her father has AIS, but her mother does not. The man (&male;) has HD. The father (&male;) of the man (&male;) does not have HD. The woman (&female;) does not have HD.</p><p>Reminder: AIS is X-linked recessive and HD is autosomal dominant.</p><p>What fraction of their daughters (&female;) will have neither AIS nor HD?</p>
PROMPT_0F40_E69F
loadMacros('parserRadioButtons.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_0F40_E69F_CHOICE_1';
None, 0%
LITERAL_0F40_E69F_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_0F40_E69F_CHOICE_2';
1/4, 25%
LITERAL_0F40_E69F_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_0F40_E69F_CHOICE_3';
1/2, 50%
LITERAL_0F40_E69F_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_0F40_E69F_CHOICE_4';
3/4, 75%
LITERAL_0F40_E69F_CHOICE_4
$choice_5 = <<'LITERAL_0F40_E69F_CHOICE_5';
All, 100%
LITERAL_0F40_E69F_CHOICE_5
$correct_1 = <<'LITERAL_0F40_E69F_CORRECT_1';
1/4, 25%
LITERAL_0F40_E69F_CORRECT_1
@choices = ($choice_1, $choice_2, $choice_3, $choice_4, $choice_5);
$answer = RadioButtons([@choices], $correct_1, labels => 'ABC', displayLabels => 1, randomize => 0, noindex => 1, separator => '<div style="margin-bottom: 0.7em;"></div>');
TEXT(MODES(HTML => $prompt, TeX => ''));
BEGIN_TEXT
\{$answer->buttons\}
END_TEXT
